(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[14 1 "// The module _signal (PY6f; Modules/signalmodule.c): the process's signals delivered to Python handlers."] [15 1 "// signal(n, callable) has os/signal notify one channel; its receiver goroutine marks the signal pending (the C"] [16 1 "// handler's trip_signal), sets the eval breaker, wakes the main thread when it blocks and writes the wakeup fd;"] [17 1 "// the main thread runs the handlers at its next check (thread_gil.go). SIG_IGN is signal.Ignore, SIG_DFL"] [18 1 "// signal.Reset. raise_signal and os.kill of the own process run the handler before they return, as on Linux."] [19 1 "// The interval timers (alarm, setitimer) are Go timers sending the signal; pthread_sigmask's mask is kept here:"] [20 1 "// a blocked signal stays pending (sigpending, sigwait) until unblocked."] [26 1 "// sysPidfdSendSignal is pidfd_send_signal's syscall number (424 on linux/amd64 and linux/arm64)"] [31 39 "// the main thread's wake-up from a blocking wait"] [32 39 "// any arrival (sigwait)"] [33 39 "// tripped, its handler to run"] [34 39 "// is_tripped"] [35 39 "// pthread_sigmask's mask"] [36 39 "// arrived while blocked (sigpending)"] [37 39 "// notified on sigCh"] [38 39 "// arrivals so far (pidfd_send_signal's wait)"] [39 39 "// set_wakeup_fd's fd, -1 none"] [40 39 "// set_wakeup_fd's warn_on_full_buffer"] [41 39 "// the errno of a failed write to the wakeup fd, its report pending (0 none)"] [43 2 "// sigHandlers are the Python-level handlers (Handlers[n].func), touched under the GIL"] [45 21 "// default_int_handler"] [51 2 "// SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored at the start, before any import of signal, as CPython's _PySignal_Init does with"] [52 2 "// install_signal_handlers (py-design-1122: a write to a closed pipe is a BrokenPipeError, json.tool's exit status"] [53 2 "// EPIPE, not the signal's death); _signal's import records them as SIG_IGN"] [57 1 "// blockedMask is the running thread's pthread_sigmask mask as a kernel sigset (py-mp-