aise_and_yield_from killed the driver, status 130)"] [236 33 "// musl's raise is tkill"] [241 1 "// tripSignal marks n pending and wakes the main thread (trip_signal)."] [253 1 "// runPendingSignals is _PyErr_CheckSignalsTstate on the main thread: each tripped signal's Python handler"] [254 1 "// called with the signal and the running frame; an exception from one leaves the rest tripped for later."] [263 2 "// _Py_HandlePending: the signals' handlers, then the pending calls (a failed wakeup write's report); a handler's"] [264 2 "// exception leaves the report for the next check (sigAny kept)"] [276 4 "// no Python handler by the time the check runs (bpo-43406): interrupt_main's tripped signal after"] [277 4 "// _PySignal_Fini, or a handler replaced since; an unraisable error, never the signal's action"] [298 1 "// signalFini is _PySignal_Fini (Py_FinalizeEx's, before finalize_modules: queue 595, test_signal's"] [299 1 "// test__thread_interrupt_main): every handler cleared and its tripped mark dropped, a Python handler's signal back to"] [300 1 "// its default action; a __del__ at the modules' clearing that calls interrupt_main then finds no handler (the race"] [301 1 "// condition's unraisable OSError, runPendingSignals)."] [317 1 "// setOSHandler makes the process's action for n follow its Python handler and the mask: notified when a"] [318 1 "// callable handles it or it is blocked, else ignored or the default."] [342 3 "// SIG_DFL is the default action, also for a signal ignored at the start that Go's Reset leaves ignored"] [343 3 "// (py-mods-1122)"] [350 1 "// exitSigint is Modules/main.c's exit_sigint after an unhandled KeyboardInterrupt (queue 231): SIGINT's default action"] [351 1 "// restored and the signal sent to the process, so that its parent sees it killed by SIGINT; else exit status 130."] [357 38 "// delivered to this thread on the call's return; another one's at the latest here"] [362 1 "// killSignal is kill(pid, sig). The own process's signal with a Python handler, not blocked, is delivered here"] [363 1 "// and its handler run before kill returns, as the kernel delivers it to the calling thread before kill returns"] [364 1 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches the handler)."] [379 3 "// blocked: pending when kill returns, as the kernel makes it (queue 231: sigpending right after saw nothing, the"] [380 3 "// signal still on its way through Go's handler thread)"] [390 1 "// the interval timers (ITIMER_REAL, ITIMER_VIRTUAL, ITIMER_PROF), counted in wall time"] [404 1 "// setItimer arms which's timer (value 0 disarms), returning the old value and interval."] [423 3 "// disarmed: an expiry not yet handled is dropped, as the kernel's single pending bit is taken by the"] [424 3 "// handler that disarms it"] [445 5 "// a Python handler: delivered here, under the timer's lock, so a disarmed timer sends no more"] [446 5 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches it)"] [475 2 "// the start installs SIGINT's handler (py-os-1124; pylifecycle's init_signals, _PySignal_Init: a program that never"] [476 2 "// imports signal ends with KeyboardInterrupt at a SIGINT, not by the signal; test_subprocess's test_send_signal)"] [497 4 "// as at CPython's start: SIGINT's default_int_handler, SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored, the rest SIG_DFL"] [503 4 "// a SIGHUP ignored at the process's start (nohup, a parent's SIG_IGN): SIG_IGN, as CPython's signal_get_set_handlers"] [504 4 "// reads it (py-mods-1122)"] [509 4 "// SIGINT's default_int_handler, unless the process started with SIGINT ignored (signal_install_handlers sets it"] [510 4 "// only over SIG_DFL: a child of nohup or of a SIG_IGN keeps ignoring it)"] [630 5 "// the C handler runs inside raise(): the Python handler before raise_signal returns"] [653 4 "// set_wakeup_fd(fd, /, *, warn_on_full_buffer=True)"] [773 5 "// only the main thread runs handlers: wait for any arrival"] [777 4 "// until a signal is pending (a stale wake-up token